 cluster is running across node1, node2, and node3, all serving.\",\"status\":\"not_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Node3 never had mariadb started at any point in the timeline after packages/config were installed (cmd-89239ac15f614ed7 only installed lsof/rsync; no subsequent rc-service mariadb start on node3 appears). Node1 and node2 repeatedly failed SST (rsync SST 'terminated unexpectedly' errors on cmd-0706289e7be24c5f, cmd-d674c7171351425f, cmd-95161db928b94c32, cmd-8c2f3d87a48a4f27, cmd-5da1c2f7ca364caa; later mariabackup SST failed with 'wsrep_sst_mariabackup: line 742: [: too many arguments' per cmd-418cd489ff114dce). At the final observed state (after_executor snapshot), node1 has mariadbd listening alone on 4567 with no confirmed cluster_size>1, node2 has no mariadbd process running, and node3 was never brought into the cluster at all. Three members serving was never achieved.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-4cb69cd671a148ee\",\"cmd-89239ac15f614ed7\",\"cmd-0706289e7be24c5f\",\"cmd-95161db928b94c32\",\"cmd-8c2f3d87a48a4f27\",\"cmd-418cd489ff114dce\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\"]},{\"id\":\"R2-application-data-present\",\"requirement\":\"The cluster holds application data (committed writes) that must survive the maintenance window.\",\"status\":\"not_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"No command in the full timeline creates a database, table, or inserts application data of any kind. Only administrative actions (root password reset, SST configuration) touch the mysql system schema. There is no baseline write to verify persistence against.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-18684607ba454e2a\",\"cmd-efa8fa08af6a430d\"]},{\"id\":\"R3-full-shutdown-for-maintenance\",\"requirement\":\"The cluster is brought down completely for a maintenance window (as a deliberate, bounded operation).\",\"status\":\"not_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"The only full-cluster stop/kill sequences observed (e.g., cmd-a4c5ea077a284857 wiping node1 datadir, cmd-1f1ff779439a48d1 wiping node2, cmd-b376aba589434797 wiping node3, and the earlier kill -9/pkill cycles on node2) were troubleshooting resets after failed SST attempts, not a deliberate, coordinated maintenance-window shutdown of a previously healthy 3-node cluster. A healthy 3-node baseline was never reached before these stops, so this cannot be scored as a bounded disruption of a working cluster.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a4c5ea077a284857\",\"cmd-1f1ff779439a48d1\",\"cmd-b376aba589434797\",\"cmd-3405e29e95f043ac\",\"cmd-f87acbf17dab46fd\"]},{\"id\":\"R4-recovery-with-writes-and-all-members\",\"requirement\":\"After maintenance, the cluster is restored with every committed write intact and all three members serving again.\",\"status\":\"not_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"No recovery cycle was ever completed. The executor's final command (cmd-bfb4da97f0634eee, installing coreutils/timeout) occurs immediately before the 1200-second timeout, with node2 mariadbd crashed from a failed mariabackup SST and node3 never having run mariadb at all. There is no evidence of a full down state followed by a full 3-node up state, nor any data verification.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bfb4da97f0634eee\",\"cmd-b3709d06929146dc\",\"global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets\"]}],\"confidence\":0.85,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.25,\"summary\":\"The executor performed many state-changing actions during an unresolved 20-minute troubleshooting loop. Several were bounded/necessary (initial apk installs of mariadb/galera/rsync/lsof/mariadb-backup/coreutils across all nodes: cmd-ff1391c5953e4503, cmd-69a78501f68f40df, cmd-f4924331209b4c27, cmd-abf718334a9d446c, cmd-d8ff80a2f43847d9, cmd-89239ac15f614ed7, cmd-61d2fb6d1e5a47f3, cmd-ba58eefd88f14cec, cmd-4f44bbcfccd7440d, cmd-bfb4da97f0634eee; galera.cnf writes: cmd-4fda698c0be34b2b, cmd-91e9c9d2fcc74ee1, cmd-d1970a20794e4c25). However, repeated full datadir wipes on node1/node2/node3 